A wide boat comes across the water.
It is the harbour bus.
The boat sails in to the wooden pier.
It stops at the edge.
I am going with the harbour bus now.
I step on board the ship.
I scan my blue travel card again.
Many passengers sit inside.
But I walk out onto the open deck.
I stand at the very front.
We sail with the boat across the blue water.
The city looks beautiful from the water.
The sun shines down on us.
I take a deep breath.
The air is very fresh and cold.
I enjoy the short trip.
We are soon over at the other side.
